#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# dirichlet_l

#% text
# `dirichlet_l(k, j, s)` gives the Dirichlet L-function of the character with modulus `k` and Conrey label `j`: `k^(-s)` times the sum of `chi(a) zeta(s, a/k)`. Evaluated for inexact `s` (machine precision); `k = 1` is the zeta function.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
dirichlet_l(4, 3, 2.)
#% output
#= 0.9159655941772189

#% cell
dirichlet_l(1, 1, 2)
#% output
#= (1/6)*pi^2

#% cell
dirichlet_l(3, 2, 1.5)
#% output
#= 0.7039682448687328

#% cell
dirichlet_l(2, 1, 1. + sqrt(-1))
#% output
#= 0.6543589174072333 - 0.3843763502147998im

